# S1: smoke the PRODUCTION profile on the window's image after an all-four reset. This change set leaves production byte for byte what it was (dflash_traced_publish
# is changed only for the four-card sibling cache and only when QWEN_FAST_TRACED_PUBLISH=1, which the production profile sets to 0), so this must behave as the
# last production smoke did. Read: no '[PACKED-PUBLISH] fusion=declined' line, no '[PACKED-FUSED]' line, no lever marker anywhere in the container log;
# '[PINDIAG] packed-any admission passed:' and no UNQUALIFIED line; no late prefill program; c2_smoke_check clean; every concurrent user at 800 tokens; every
# concurrent4 hash equal to its concurrent4_solo run; speed within 5% of the previous production smoke. Any difference is this branch's: STOP.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1 to 3 min, engine build 10 to 20 min on a warm cache, the smoke 15 to 25 min: 60 min at most.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-scope window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-scope and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3m is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3m
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,tool_call,stream_tool_call,stream_reasoning,refused_n2,alive_after_refusal,stream_dropped,alive_after_drop,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4_code,concurrent4_code_equal
